LiftKit bundles three reference databases. Each carries its own terms, and
they are kept in separate files so that no obligation spreads to another.

  Sources/LiftReference/Resources/food.db
    U.S. Department of Agriculture, FoodData Central. Public domain.

  Sources/LiftReference/Resources/exercises.db
    free-exercise-db. Public domain.
    wger. CC BY-SA 3.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

  Sources/LiftReference/Resources/recipes.db
    UniTools World Recipes — theunitools.com
    CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

    Pennsylvania Dutch Cooking (Project Gutenberg #26558). Public domain.

    Built by Tools/build_recipes.py. Every row records its own license and
    attribution; the public-domain rows remain public domain. The file as a
    whole is distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0 because it contains BY-SA rows.
    LiftKit's code is Apache-2.0, which is not share-alike, so the
    database stays a separate file: anything adapted from it stays CC BY-SA.

    ReferenceDatabase.recipeAttributions() returns these credits so the apps
    can show them. CC BY-SA requires the credit to be given; it must stay
    reachable from the UI.

LiftKit's street maps (map/) are drawn from files the person downloads.

  map/fonts/
    Noto Sans Regular glyphs. SIL Open Font License 1.1; the license text
    is map/fonts/OFL.txt.

  Street data
    © OpenStreetMap contributors. Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 —
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
    Vector tiles from OpenFreeMap — https://openfreemap.org
    Every map shows "© OpenStreetMap contributors · OpenFreeMap".

  MapLibre
    MapLibre Native (iOS, Android): BSD-2-Clause.
    MapLibre GL JS (web): BSD-3-Clause.
